Fix for kocurvik/threeview @ b43383efba129b8d90e2709092dac6dc87cbbea1 (Tzamos et al. CVPR 2025 eval code),
applied by scripts/build_seed_code.sh.

The published Aachen triplets (Zenodo 16603086) name images like 'db/123.jpg'; HDF5 stores those as
nested groups, but eval.py and get_camera_dicts read K.h5 / R.h5 / T.h5 with File.items(), which only
sees the top-level groups ("IndexError: too many indices for array" on Aachen). Read every dataset
recursively instead; PhotoTourism files are flat, so their results are unchanged.

